<section class="page-top section-tight" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap page-head wide">
    <h1 id="how-title">Diagnosis first. Then the work gets done.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kevin reads your numbers and puts the fixes in order. Then the system runs the repeat work each day, and the weekly read shows what changed.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="both-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <h2 id="both-title" class="split-head">Most brands get one or the other.</h2>
    <dl class="rows">
      <div>
        <dt>Diagnosis</dt>
        <dd>A person reads what is public about your ads, store, offer, retention and tracking, plus your answers, and tells you the truth about them. Advice alone leaves the work on your desk.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Execution</dt>
        <dd>A system that does the repeat work every day, so repeat work does not wait on a busy team. Work without a diagnosis fixes the wrong things first.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Freeland</dt>
        <dd>Both, in that order. The read decides what the system works on.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="steps-title">The three steps</h2>
    <ol class="ladder">
      <li class="ladder-step">
        <h3>Growth Roadmap</h3>
        <p><strong>Free. You keep it either way.</strong> You apply with five answers and pick a time. Kevin starts from your public store and ads plus your answers and puts the leaks in order, with where to start. On a 30-minute call he walks you through your roadmap. A deeper read of your accounts needs view access, agreed on the call. Then you decide whether we do the work or you do it yourself.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="ladder-step">
        <h3>We run the fixes</h3>
        <p>If you want us to do the work, it is scoped for your brand: ads, landing pages, retention and automation, on one plan, with Kevin making the calls.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="ladder-step">
        <h3>It keeps running</h3>
        <p>The system keeps running after the first fixes. Each week you get a plain-English read: what moved, why, and the next three moves.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section rule-top">
<div class="wrap stack-v">
<h2>What Freeland is responsible for</h2>
<p class="lede">Who does what once we work together.</p>
<div class="responsibility-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Responsibilities" tabindex="0">
