<section class="section rule-top" aria-labelledby="team-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <h2 id="team-title" class="split-head">How we work with your team</h2>
    <ul class="rows">
      <li>
        <h3>You talk to Kevin</h3>
        <p>Not an account manager. Kevin reads the numbers himself and makes the calls.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Access starts small</h3>
        <p>The roadmap needs your store address and five answers. For the deeper read, view-only access to your ad accounts and store reports, agreed on the call. Changes wait for your say-so.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Next to the people you have</h3>
        <p>Already have an agency or an in-house team? The roadmap is a second opinion you keep. You can use it to check what your current team is doing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>You see what changed</h3>
        <p>The weekly read says what changed and why, in plain English. No dashboards to decode.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
